    tc_diag(id, "E0643", "'" + nm + "' cannot take bytes: argument " + i + " is bytes; a byte buffer is binary, not text -- write print(string_of_bytes(b)) to print it as text (it stops if a byte is 0), or write its elements one at a time", nm, "bytes is binary, so there is nothing for " + nm + " to write as text", "write " + nm + "(string_of_bytes(b)) to print it as text, or write its elements one at a time");
